  "body": "## What\n\nTwo related UI improvements, built with the `/ui-ux-pro-max:ui-ux-pro-max` skill.\n\n### 1. Claude Code config moves to a dedicated page\nThe Claude Code settings card lived on the Providers page, competing with 30+ provider cards. It now has its own **\"Claude Code\"** nav view (between Providers and Model Config), with a page heading explaining the one-click Configure flow.\n- New `claude` view in `VIEW_GROUPS` (static view, like Get Started/Guide, so the view-registry guard is safe).\n- The `claudeSettingsPanel` section moved from `#view-providers` into a new `#view-claude` admin-view section.\n- `loadClaudeSettings()` refreshes when the Claude page is activated (like web_search does).\n- Onboarding \"Point Claude Code at MCC\" step now targets `view=\"claude\"`; Guide step 1 now says \"Open the Claude Code page from the left nav.\"\n\n### 2. Theme picker consistency\nThe selected pill used `background: var(--accent)` — a full accent fill that recolored per theme (emerald on midnight, crimson on velvet) and read as a broken, uneven control. It now uses the theme's **neutral raised surface** (`--panel-strong`) with an **accent ring + accent text** — identical structure across all four themes (Midnight / Paper / High Contrast / Velvet).\n\n## Verification (real browser, throwaway server :8165, fake home)\n\n- Nav shows \"Claude Code\" between Providers and Model Config.\n- Clicking it: activeView \"Claude Code\", view visible, Configure/Remove/path controls present.\n- Providers page no longer contains `#claudeSettingsPanel`; still has Version + Custom providers.\n- Selected theme pill: midnight → `bg rgb(23,27,38)` + `color rgb(16,185,129)`; velvet → `bg rgb(19,29,48)` + `color rgb(230,67,94)` — structurally identical, no full accent fill.\n- **The view-registry guard caught a real break:** onboarding step `view` targets are pinned in a hardcoded set in `tests/config/test_onboarding.py`; `claude` had to be added there.\n- Full suite: 3706 passed, 26 known environmental failures (identical baseline), 26 skipped. ruff format/check + ty all clean.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The Guide \"Point Codex or Pi here\" section and the troubleshooting section still reference Providers legitimately (they're about providers, not Claude Code config).\n- Desktop/terminal screenshots in the Guide still show the old UI (documented in the previous docs PR).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
