    "message": "feat(admin): move Claude Code config to a dedicated page + consistent theme picker\n\nThe Claude Code settings card lived on the Providers page, where it competed\nwith 30+ provider cards and was easy to lose. It now has its own \"Claude Code\"\nnav view (between Providers and Model Config), with a page heading that\nexplains the one-click Configure flow. The onboarding \"Point Claude Code at\nMCC\" step and the Guide now route to the new page.\n\nAlso fixed the theme picker: the selected pill used a full accent fill, so it\nrecolored per theme (emerald on midnight, crimson on velvet) and read as a\nbroken, uneven control. The selected state is now the theme's neutral raised\nsurface with an accent ring — identical structure across all four themes.\n\nVerified in a real browser on a throwaway server: the Claude Code nav item\nappears, its page renders the Configure/Remove/path controls, the Providers\npage no longer contains the section, and the selected pill is neutral+accent\nunder both midnight and velvet. The view-registry guard caught that onboarding\nstep view targets are pinned in a hardcoded set — 'claude' added. Full suite:\n3706 passed, 26 known environmental failures, zero new regressions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
